< The important features above are the "x"s in the first column. Those are execute bits for owner, group, and world. They are part of the file permissions, set by the "chmod" command. Most FTP servers don't support "chmod", so you'll [http://www.pureteenz.com/weight-loss/ weight loss] need to do it in a unix shell (not supported by most web service [http://www.pureteenz.com/Aria-Giovanni/ Aria Giovanni] providers) or by using a control panel page. If your provider has no such thing, it's probably because you don't need it; the execute bits will be properly set when you upload the script. Set the file permissions [http://www.plazaerotica.com/manga/ manga] to 755 (octal for the read/write/execute bit of each of owner/group/world, so 7 is "rwx" & 5 is "r-x"), though it appears that 750 works on my provider.
